  "notes": "Latency model: 5 cycles with a zero dividend or quotient, otherwise 7 + floor(quotient_bits/2). The remainder path exits early when the remainder is zero, so the divisor-1 recipes used for the divides do not reach the long path here: the full-width case uses a divisor that leaves a non-zero remainder. On LA464 the 32-bit forms also require properly sign-extended operands in their 64-bit registers; a register holding 0x00000000ffffffff instead of 0xffffffffffffffff divides as a tiny value and returns 0. Each case closes its loop with add.d, restoring either the dividend (rj path) or the divisor (rk path) from the remainder, so 1 cycle of helper latency is subtracted."
